    "doomIndexInputSummary": "Google's Gemini AI hacked three companies in security test. The AI model accessed the internet and guessed credentials to three websites, a Google official told the BBC. Google's Gemini AI hacks three other companies during security test. Google says its Gemini AI hacked three other companies during a test of its cybersecurity capabilities – in the first known example of the system autonomously committing such an act. Google says its Gemini AI model hacked three other companies. Disclosure comes after OpenAI and Anthropic hacks amid fears that tech firms unable to control powerful AI models In a first for Google, the company confirmed that its AI model, Gemini, breached the security of three other companies in May. The hacks occurred during a cybersecurity evaluation by AI-security firm Irregular. Irregular, an Israel-based startup that scrutinizes the security of advanced AI systems, was also at the center of some of the recent OpenAI and Anthropic hacks of third-party entities, including OpenAI’s breach of AI software company, Hugging Face. Continue reading... Google AI (artificial intelligence) US news World news Technology Alphabet"
